// expect: 123
// A PARENTHESIZED FANOUT INSIDE A FANOUT IS FLATTENED. The author grouped
// `(1) >< (2)` and fanned the pair out beside `(3)`, so the value is
// ((1, 2), 3). The program refuses with E_TypeMismatch (measured 2026-09-25)
// because the parser's N-ary accretion folds the inner fanout's branches
// into the outer one and yields a 3-tuple. The N-ary law covers an
// unparenthesized chain; parentheses are the author's grouping.
//
// Retires when accretion stops at the author's parentheses.
fn main() = {
  let t = ((1) >< (2)) >< (3)
  match t {
    ((a, b), c) => a * 100 + b * 10 + c,
  }
}
